// One line of a detail panel: a step and its count, a reward and its picture, or a reason
// something is out of reach. ONE template for all three, because the three differ in what they SAY
// rather than in what they are, and a page that appended three near-identical templates would be
// three places to fix a spacing change. Appended into a panel's list container and addressed via
// the INDEXED PARENT ("#MyList[0] #LineText").
//
// It lives in this module because more than one module appends it - the objective book's giver
// screen and the storefront and board pages all do - and a second copy beside one of those callers
// would ship at the same asset path as this one, so only one of the two would ever reach a client.
//
// The icon slot is hidden until a line has a picture to show. A line with nothing behind it (a
// payout of experience, a step that asks for a whole family of blocks) renders as its text alone
// rather than borrowing an unrelated thing's picture, which would read as a promise of that thing.
//
// Two sibling widgets, exactly one of which is ever visible, both driven by ui/icon/IconRenderer:
// #IcoItem draws an item's own generated icon from a plain item id, and #IcoTex draws a
// Common-rooted texture path - which is how a creature is shown, from the still the client renders
// of it. #IcoTex carries a fallback so a creature that never had one rendered still lines up.
//
// All text lands on #LineText.TextSpans: a Message on a Label's .Text neither substitutes {0} nor
// renders markup.

Group #ZigDetailLine {
  LayoutMode: Left;
  Anchor: (Height: 26, Bottom: 2);

  Group #LineIconSlot {
    Anchor: (Width: 24, Height: 24, Right: 8);
    Visible: false;

    ItemIcon #IcoItem {
      Anchor: (Width: 24, Height: 24);
      Visible: false;
    }

    AssetImage #IcoTex {
      Anchor: (Width: 24, Height: 24);
      Visible: false;
      FallbackTexturePath: "UI/Custom/Pages/Memories/MissingIcon.png";
    }
  }

  Label #LineText {
    FlexWeight: 1;
    Text: "";
    Style: (FontSize: 14, TextColor: #c6d4e4, VerticalAlignment: Center);
  }
}
